  equal: in 24 of 24 trained A / ZY circuits at least one qubit has a marginal of exactly 0.5 (a qubit that is only ever a control cannot leave 50/50); with an unequal share that caps the probability of a unique optimum at 0.5. Variant A+ (our extension) adds one ry per qubit to remove the cap.
  cpu_gpu: in 24 of 24 trained A / ZY circuits at least one qubit has a marginal of exactly 0.5 (a qubit that is only ever a control cannot leave 50/50); with an unequal share that caps the probability of a unique optimum at 0.5. Variant A+ (our extension) adds one ry per qubit to remove the cap.
  IonQ batch: 96 final trained circuits with measurement are stored in `varqite_ionq_circuits` for the single IonQ job (with the p = 0 control and the QAOA circuits). Training stays local and noiseless; only the final sampling is meant for the IonQ Forte 1 noise model.
  fairness note: varQITE spends steps x (2m + 1) training circuits with EXACT expectations (on hardware each would need shots); the optimised QAOA variants used at most 200 evaluations, LR-QAOA none.
